    "## 🔧 Tracking System Fixes Applied\n",
    "\n",
    "### Issues Fixed:\n",
    "1. **Indentation Problems** - Fixed all Python indentation errors in tracking classes\n",
    "2. **Track ID Assignment** - Fixed logic for assigning target IDs to tracks based on spatial overlap\n",
    "3. **Track Recovery** - Added system to recover lost tracks with same target ID\n",
    "4. **CLIP Threshold** - Lowered threshold from 0.25 to 0.20 for better matching\n",
    "5. **Tracking Parameters** - Optimized for better consistency:\n",
    "   - IoU threshold: 0.25 (lower for crowded scenes)\n",
    "   - ReID threshold: 0.5 (more forgiving)\n",
    "   - Min hits: 2 (faster confirmation)\n",
    "   - Max lost frames: 15 (faster cleanup)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Improvements:\n",
    "- **Spatial Matching**: Track-to-target assignment now uses IoU overlap validation\n",
    "- **Target Persistence**: Lost tracks can be recovered if same target reappears\n",
    "- **Better Debugging**: Enhanced logging to track assignment process\n",
    "- **Detection Mapping**: Proper mapping between detections and target IDs\n",
    "\n",
    "### Expected Results:\n",
    "- More consistent track IDs for same person\n",
    "- Better handling of temporary occlusions\n",
    "- Reduced false positives in crowded scenes\n",
    "- Improved target re-identification across frames\n",
    "\n",
    "### Next Steps:\n",
    "1. Run the initialization cells in order (cells 1-14)\n",
    "2. Configure your target descriptions in the configuration cell\n",
    "3. Run the main tracking execution\n",
    "4. The system should now maintain consistent track IDs"
